---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Tally"
  description="Tally processes all screen-time data on your device. No account, no servers, no analytics."
>
  <Nav />

  <main class="wrap doc" id="main">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: July 12, 2026</p>

    <p>
      Tally is built so that we couldn’t see your data even if we wanted to.
      This page explains what that means in practice.
    </p>

    <h2>What Tally collects</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. Tally is free, and it has no account system, no analytics
      SDK, no ads, and no backend servers. We do not collect, store, transmit, or sell any personal
      information or usage data.
    </p>

    <h2>How screen-time data works</h2>
    <p>
      Tally uses Apple’s Screen Time framework (the Family Controls,
      Device Activity, and Managed Settings APIs) to measure app usage and
      enforce limits. Apple designed these APIs so that usage data is
      processed entirely on your device, inside a sandbox the app itself has
      only limited visibility into. Your app activity never leaves your
      iPhone.
    </p>

    <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The limits and rules you create</li>
      <li>Your usage history and statistics</li>
      <li>Your override history</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      All of it lives in local storage on your iPhone. Deleting the app
      deletes this data.
    </p>

    <h2>Third parties</h2>
    <p>
      Tally embeds no third-party trackers, ad networks, or analytics tools.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy ever changes, the updated version will be posted on this
      page with a new date. Because Tally has no way to contact you, we
      recommend checking back after major app updates.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy? Email
      <a href="mailto:dmytro.bohachevskyy@gmail.com">dmytro.bohachevskyy@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .doc {
    max-width: 720px;
    padding-top: 80px;
    padding-bottom: 96px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 40px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .updated {
    color: var(--text-faint);
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-top: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-top: 44px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  p {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  ul {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    padding-left: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--indigo);
  }

  a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
